# Kernels: sad_snapshot_sweep
#
# The pass a save runs over each texture it is about to take, one dispatch a
# texture, leaving a word a chunk in `flags`. SaSadClearChunks, beside this,
# dispatches it and reads the words back where the save reads back already.
#
# The word of the chunk is set when any texel of the texture differs from the
# blank that field opens at, compared bit for bit and never within a
# tolerance, so a chunk whose word stays zero holds nothing in any field the
# pass was run over and the save leaves it out. A hash is never compared with
# a blank chunk's hash, because a collision there would delete paint.
#
# Only the first `channels` channels are compared, since a fetch answers zero
# and one for the channels a format does not have. The pass reads and never
# writes the texture, and a set word is only ever set again, so lanes that
# store into the same word at once store the same value.
#
# Any other output a save wants of the same textures, such as a hash a field
# for the reuse of unchanged chunks, is one more output of this kernel rather
# than a second pass.

kernel sad_snapshot_sweep

sampler field

# One word a chunk, zeroed before the first dispatch and set by any texel that
#   differs from its field's blank.
buffer flags: uint words[]

params:
    vec4 blank
    int width
    int height
    int channels
    int slot


@workgroup_size(8, 8)
def sad_snapshot_sweep():
    if pixel.x >= width or pixel.y >= height:
        return
    vec4 texel = texel_fetch(field, pixel, 0)
    for channel in range(4):
        if channel < channels and float_bits_to_uint(texel[channel]) != float_bits_to_uint(blank[channel]):
            flags.words[slot] = 1u
